[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Asking for Trouble]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.40]Why did the policeman ask the writer to come to the police station? | 为什么警察要求作者去警察局？
[00:17.41]It must have been about two in the morning when I returned home. | 我回到家时肯定已是凌晨两点左右了。
[00:22.77]I tried to wake up my wife by ringing the doorbell, | 我按门铃想唤醒妻子，
[00:26.83]but she was fast asleep, | 但她睡得很沉，
[00:29.25]so I got a ladder from the shed in the garden, put it against the wall, | 于是我从花园的棚子里拿来一架梯子，把它靠在墙上，
[00:34.71]and began climbing towards the bedroom window. | 开始向卧室的窗户爬去。
[00:38.60]I was almost there when a sarcastic voice below said. | 快爬到窗户时，下面一个人用讽刺的口吻说：
[00:44.36]'I don't think the windows need cleaning at this time of the night.' | “我想不必在夜里这个时候擦窗户吧。”
[00:50.07]I looked down and nearly fell off the ladder when I saw a policeman. | 我朝下看了看，一看到是个警察，差一点从梯子上掉下去。
[00:56.45]I immediately regretted answering in the way I did, but I said, 'I enjoy cleaning windows at night.' | 我立刻后悔不该那样回答，但我还是说了：“我就喜欢夜里擦窗户。”
[01:07.86]'So do I,' answered the policeman in the same tone. | “我也喜欢，”警察用同样的声调回答说。
[01:13.36]Excuse my interrupting you. | 请原谅我打断了您。
[01:16.20]I hate to interrupt a man when he's busy working, but would you mind coming with me to the station?' | 我不愿意在一个人忙着干活时打断他，但您介意跟我到警察局去一趟吗？”
[01:25.82]'Well, I'd prefer to stay here,' I said. | “哦，我想留在这儿，”我说。
[01:30.64]'You see, I've forgotten my key.' | “您瞧，我忘带钥匙了。”
[01:34.12]'Your what?' he called. | “你的什么？”他喊道。
[01:37.11]'My key,' I shouted. | “我的钥匙，”我大声喊。
[01:41.21]Fortunately, the shouting woke up my wife who opened the window just as the policeman had started to climb towards me. | 幸运的是，喊声惊醒了我的妻子。就在警察开始朝我爬上来时，她打开了窗子。
